.TH ALLOCATOR_TRIM 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
allocator_trim \- retry releasing retained allocator mappings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdlib.h>
.PP
.B int allocator_trim();
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR allocator_trim ()
retries unmapping unused storage retained after an allocator cleanup failure:
large replacement mappings retained during failed
.BR realloc (3crunch)
rollback and completely empty pool arenas whose release failed.
It does not release or move live allocations.
.PP
The function attempts every eligible mapping even if one unmap fails.
Successfully unmapped entries are removed; entries that still cannot be
unmapped remain available for reuse and can be retried by a later call.
There is no guarantee of a memory limit if unmapping continues to fail.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero means all eligible mappings were released, or none were retained.
On success,
.B errno
is unchanged.
If any unmap fails, the function returns \-1 and sets
.B errno
to the first unmap error. Other entries may still have been released.
.SH NOTES
This is a Crunch\-specific operation, not the C library's
.BR malloc_trim .
The allocator is not thread\-safe, and Crunch
.B errno
is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR malloc (3crunch),
.BR realloc (3crunch),
.BR free (3crunch),
.BR munmap (2),
.BR crunch (1)
